missing_sensors.description:
These sensors are set in the integration but do not exist in Home Assistant, or the learned planner is in control without one it needs:

{sensors}

Until they are there the planners treat their readings as missing; nothing is charged on a guess. Pick the right sensors under Settings, Devices and services, Solarseed Peak Shaver, Configure, Battery and sensors. This notice clears itself within ten minutes of the fix.

no_automations.description:
The planner in control fires these events, and no enabled automation listens to them, so the inverter's mode will not change:

{events}

Import the three blueprints (start grid charging, stop charging, battery hold; the links are in the README), and create one automation from each with your inverter's mode entity and the value for that mode. Automations of your own triggered by these events work as well. This notice clears itself within ten minutes of the fix.
